# Line endings: every text file is stored and checked out with LF on every OS, so a checkout on Windows, macOS, Linux
# or WSL has the same bytes. Shell scripts run from WSL on a Windows checkout, and tests compare fixture files byte for
# byte. Windows tools used here (PowerShell, Inno Setup, Visual Studio, Rider) read LF files.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files are the one exception; there are none today.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary files: never converted or diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.zip binary
*.xlsx binary
*.dmg binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.p12 binary

# Preserve exact bytes of hash-pinned third-party source and notice materials.
/third-party/WeCantSpell.Hunspell/7.0.1/** -text -whitespace
